        ],
        "statement": "Assume AC and U in C^1 with 0<Z_U<infinity. The phase-space Metropolis kernel for the momentum-flipped finite leapfrog proposal preserves nu=pi x N_d(0,M). Independent momentum refresh, this phase update, and position projection define an HMC position kernel preserving pi. No mixing or convergence claim is made.",
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "axiom_use": "AC is used through the multivariate-normal density and the general Radon-Nikodym Metropolis-Hastings construction and common-submeasure supplier. The leapfrog map and its shear calculation use no arbitrary-choice principle.",
